Arguments:
	answer: ### 1. Task outcome (short version):
I retrieved and extracted all prospectus and Annual Report excerpts you provided (Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus and Link Mobility Group Holding ASA Annual Report 2020). For each document I located and compiled all sections, tables and notes that mention: Adjusted EBITDA, EBITDA, Non-GAAP measures (APMs), reconciliation, pro forma, restatement, and reconciliation tables / footnotes. I extracted definitions, historical adjusted EBITDA figures with periods, adjustment line items (M&A costs, restructuring, share-based costs), pro forma statements used for covenant testing, and auditor confirmation that the consolidated annual financial statements are audited (auditor: PwC) and that the APMs are non-IFRS and not audited. I list page/section references (as appearing in excerpts) and provide the exact snippets you provided that reference the items requested.

Summary (short):
- Prospectus (IPO prospectus): publication context is Prospectus dated around Oct 2020 (contains Six months ended 30 June 2020 and references to 31 Dec 2019 audited consolidated financial statements). APMs explicitly stated to be "not audited". Adjusted EBITDA (group) values: Six months ended 30 June 2020 = NOK 182.6m; Six months 2019 = NOK 134.2m; Year ended 31 Dec 2019 = NOK 307.5m; 2018 = NOK 212.0m; 2017 = NOK 140.0m. Adjustments listed: Share option/ program costs; M&A activities costs; Restructuring cost and other (detail in footnotes). LTM Adjusted EBITDA (LTM 30 June 2020) = 356.1. Pro forma: covenant/testing uses "LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies" (used in covenant ratios). No restatements noted in the supplied excerpts; acquisition-related estimates noted as unaudited/management estimates.
- Annual Report 2020 (audited by PwC): publication date annual report approved 26 April 2021 (notes show FY2020). Figures (audited consolidated): Adjusted EBITDA 2020 = NOK 390,841k (or 390.841 MNOK) and 2019 = NOK 307,549k; EBITDA 2020 = 293,607k; Operating profit (EBIT) 2020 = 22,218k. Adjustments: Restructuring costs 47,400k; Share-based compensation 34,711k; Expenses related to acquisitions 15,123k. Reconciliation table provided (Adjusted EBITDA to profit before tax). Auditor's report included and is unmodified; no restatement or auditor note altering historical APMs in excerpts.

### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):
Note: below I reproduce the exact extracted text snippets from the provided documents (as in your excerpts) grouped by document with locations (section / page numbers or headings as present in excerpts). Where the provenance shows the section number and page lines I include them. All figures are as reported in the excerpts; currency is NOK and many tables report values in NOK million or NOK 1,000 as indicated.

A. Prospectus (Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Prospectus)
- Publication context and audit status:
  - Section 4.2.3 "Non-IFRS financial measures" (excerpt_0; page ~18): states the APMs "are not measurements of financial performance or liquidity under IFRS ... are not audited" and investor caution. It references Section 10.7 "Non-IFRS financial measures" for reconciliation and calculation. (Location: Section 4.2.3; Prospectus page ~18 per excerpt header.)
  - Definitions glossary: Section 20 (Definitions and glossary) includes "Adjusted EBITDA -- Has the meaning ascribed to such term in Section 4.2.3" (excerpt_5; page ~127).

- Company definition of EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA and list of adjustments (exact text):
  - From Section 4.2.3 (excerpt_0):
    - "The Group defines 'EBITDA' as operating profit (loss) adding back depreciation and amortisation."
    - "The Group defines 'Adjusted EBITDA' as EBITDA adjusted for mergers and acquisitions costs, restructuring costs and costs related to share option program."
    - "The Group defines 'Adjusted EBITDA Margin' as Adjusted EBITDA as a percentage of operating revenues in the respective periods."
    - Also defines LTM Adjusted EBITDA, Gross Profit Conversion (Adjusted EBITDA divided by Gross Profit), Like-for-Like Revenue, etc.
    (Location: Section 4.2.3)

- Exact historical adjusted EBITDA values reported (tables):
  - Section 10.7.1 Non-IFRS financial measures for the Group (excerpt_2 / excerpt_1 / excerpt_4). Table (In NOK million):
    - Six months ended 30 June 2020: EBITDA 160.0; Adjusted EBITDA 182.6
    - Six months ended 30 June 2019: EBITDA 83.4; Adjusted EBITDA 134.2
    - Year ended 31 December 2019: EBITDA 210.4; Adjusted EBITDA 307.5
    - Year ended 31 December 2018: Adjusted EBITDA 212.0
    - Year ended 31 December 2017: Adjusted EBITDA 140.0
    - LTM Adjusted EBITDA (LTM ended 30 June 2020): 356.1
    (Locations: Section 10.7.1 table; Prospectus page ~54 / ~78 / ~23 depending on excerpt)
  - Segment-level Adjusted EBITDA (10.7.2 / excerpt_2 & excerpt_3): totals match 182.645 (NOK 1,000 table shows 182,645 for six months 2020 which aligns with 182.6 NOKm). By segment for six months 30 June 2020:
    - Nordics: 118,942 (NOK 1,000 => 118.942m)
    - Central Europe: 57,945
    - Western Europe: 55,118
    - Global Messaging: 12,442
    - Group Costs: -61,802
    - Total: 182,645
    (Location: Section 10.7.2)

- Reconciliation tables and adjustments detail (exact excerpts):
  - Reconciliation between operating profit, EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA (excerpt_2/1):
    - Operating profit: 53 (30 Jun 2020), -20 (30 Jun 2019), -37 (YE2019), 30 (2018), 45 (2017)
    - Depreciation & amortisation: 108, 103, 247, 86, 42
    - EBITDA: 160, 83, 210, 115, 87
    - Share option program cost: 0, 0.0, 0, 23.1, 19.0
    - M&A activities costs(a): 3.3, 15.6, 27.2, 40.5, 26.0
    - Restructuring cost and other(b): 19.3, 35.2, 70.0, 33.3, 8.0
    - Total adjustments: 22.6, 50.8, 97.1, 96.9, 53.1
    - Adjusted EBITDA: 182.6, 134.2, 307.5, 212.4, 140.0
    - Footnote (a): M&A activities costs refers to consultant and legal advisor expenses related to acquisitions presented in total other operating expenses.
    - Footnote (b): restructuring cost and other represents efficiency projects, start-up costs, branding/re-branding costs; detailed amounts for six months and full year and extracts from payroll/severance highlighted (NOK figures cited). (Location: Section 10.7 notes and footnotes)

- Pro forma adjustments / covenant references:
  - Section 10 (and elsewhere) references "LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies" used in covenant testing under Senior Facilities Agreement. (excerpt_11 and excerpt_1 earlier showed covenants). Specific covenant ratios: consolidated total net debt was 7.03x LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies (31 Dec 2019 and 31 Mar 2020) vs thresholds; 6.84x at 30 June 2020. (Location: Section on Covenants; Prospectus page ~16)

- Pro forma / acquisition estimates and one-time items affecting numbers:
  - Many acquisition-related estimated revenue, gross profit and adjusted EBITDA figures for acquired entities are included (e.g., Spot-Hit, Horisen, Simple SMS, etc.) and specifically noted as "based on the Group’s estimates" and "estimates have not been subject to audit or limited review" (excerpt_3 & excerpt_4). The Prospectus describes adjustments to normalise figures to how Group would operate acquired entities. (Locations: Acquisition descriptions, Section 11.3.2 / acquisition notes)
  - The Prospectus explicitly discloses purchase price adjustments, holdbacks paid, and that some acquisition figures are management estimates (see Spot-Hit, Simple SMS, etc.). (Location: Section on acquisitions pages ~60)

- Restatements or auditor notes modifying historical figures:
  - In the Prospectus excerpts provided, I did not find any explicit restatements of historical Adjusted EBITDA or auditor-driven modifications to prior-year figures. The Prospectus emphasizes APMs are not audited and may differ between companies. Acquisition estimates are explicitly unaudited/management estimates. No auditor restatement footnote is included in the provided Prospectus excerpts.

- Locations/page references (from supplied excerpts):
  - Section 4.2.3 Non-IFRS financial measures — Prospectus excerpt_0 (page ~18)
  - Section 10.6 Revenues and Gross Profit per reporting segment — excerpt_1 (page ~54)
  - Section 10.7 Non-IFRS financial measures and reconciliation tables — excerpt_1/excerpt_2/excerpt_4 (pages ~54, ~55, ~78, ~23 in varying excerpts)
  - Footnotes (a) and (b) explaining M&A costs and restructuring costs — excerpts_2/_3
  - Covenant/pro forma EBITDA usage — excerpt_10 (page ~16)
  - Glossary definitions — excerpt_5 (page ~127)
  - Acquisition descriptions including management estimates — excerpt_3/_4 (pages ~60+)

B. Annual Report 2020 (Link Mobility Group Holding ASA - Annual Report 2020)
- Publication date and audit status:
  - The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board on 26 April 2021 (excerpt_6 / excerpt_13) — this implies the Annual Report (and audited financial statements) correspond to FY2020. Independent Auditor’s Report (PwC) included (excerpt_15 & excerpt_16), which issues an unmodified opinion asserting the consolidated financial statements give a true and fair view in accordance with IFRS as adopted by the EU. Therefore figures in the Annual Report are audited. (Locations: notes and auditor report, pages ~37 and ~98+)

- Company definition of EBITDA and Adjusted EBITDA and adjustments (exact text):
  - From APM section (excerpt_12):
    - "Adjusted EBITDA means EBITDA adjusted by expenses related to significant one-time, non-recurring events such as acquisitions and restructuring activities, legal advisors, and share-based compensation."
    - "Adjusted EBITDA margin is presented as adjusted EBITDA as a percentage of total operating revenues in the respective periods."
    - "EBITDA means earnings before interest, taxes, amortization, depreciation, and impairments." (Location: Note 25 / APMs, pages ~81-82)

- Exact historical adjusted EBITDA values reported (audited figures):
  - From APM reconciliation (excerpt_12 & excerpt_11):
    - 2020 Adjusted EBITDA: 390,841 (NOK 1,000) => 390.841 MNOK
    - 2019 Adjusted EBITDA: 307,549 (NOK 1,000) => 307.549 MNOK
    - EBITDA 2020: 293,607
    - Operating profit (EBIT) 2020: 22,218
    - Adjusted EBITDA margin 2020: 11.0% (2019: 10.6%)
    - Segment-level Adjusted EBITDA (excerpt_9): Northern Europe 240,485; Central Europe 129,283; Western Europe 127,826; Global Messaging 27,150; Group Costs -133,902; Total 390,842 (note slight rounding differences vs 390,841 in APM table). (Locations: Note 6/segment reporting and APM note)

- Reconciliation tables and adjustments detail (exact excerpts):
  - Reconciliation (excerpt_11 / excerpt_12):
    - Operating profit (EBIT) 2020: 22,218
    - Add: Depreciation intangible assets 271,389
    - EBITDA 293,607
    - Add: Restructuring costs 47,400
    - Add: Share-based compensation 34,711
    - Add: Expenses related to acquisitions 15,123
    - Adjusted EBITDA 390,841
    - Operating revenues 3,539,231 => Adjusted EBITDA margin 11.0%
  - Reconciliation of adjusted EBITDA to profit before tax (excerpt_9):
    - Adjusted EBITDA 390,842
    - Non-recurring items* -97,235
    - Depreciation & amortization -271,389
    - Operating profit 22,218
    - Finance income (expense) -427,047
    - Total -404,829 (profit/loss before tax matches -404,829k)
    - Note: *Non-recurring items list mirrors prospectus definition: M&A costs, personnel one-offs, restructuring, advisors, licenses, sales & marketing (not exhaustive).

- Pro forma adjustments or one-time items affecting numbers:
  - Annual report includes significant acquisition activity and purchase price adjustments (e.g., Purchase price adjustment acquisition of subsidiary included as a cash flow line -147,902 in FY2020 – excerpt_3). The Annual Report also shows substantial purchase price paid on acquisitions and earn-out treatments described in notes: earn-out adjustments accounted for in income statement as finance income/expense (excerpt_7 and excerpt_14). Also the Annual Report provides pro forma numbers in the Board’s forward-looking statement (pro forma revenue and pro forma adjusted EBITDA margin guidance for 2024 in excerpt_2). The covenant references in the Prospectus used "LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies" — Annual Report shows that covenant/compliance discussion is linked to facilities (prospectus excerpt_11). The Annual Report also includes purchase price adjustments as large cashflows and the FY2020 net effect (excerpt_3). These acquisition-related one-time items are explicitly included in Non-recurring items and adjustments adding back to reach Adjusted EBITDA (as shown above).

- Restatements or auditor notes modifying historical figures:
  - Auditor's report (PwC) provides an unmodified opinion (excerpt_15/16). The excerpts do not show any restatement or modified audit opinion or note that audited figures were restated. There are no explicit restatements or auditor adjustments to prior Adjusted EBITDA figures in the supplied excerpts. Note: the prospectus and annual report repeatedly state that APMs are not audited and management estimates for acquisition contributions are unaudited — these are not formal restatements but items to consider for reliability.

- Locations/page references (from supplied excerpts):
  - APMs, definitions and reconciliation: Annual Report Note 25 and pages ~81-82 (excerpt_11/_12)
  - Segment reporting with Adjusted EBITDA per segment: Note 6 and pages ~53-54 (excerpt_8/_9)
  - Cash flow and purchase price adjustments: consolidated statement of cash flows and notes - pages ~37 and related notes (excerpt_3 and excerpt_10)
  - Independent Auditor’s Report: pages ~98-99 (excerpt_15/_16)

C. Cross-document observations and issues relevant to manager:
- Audit status: Annual Report FY2020 consolidated financial statements are audited by PwC with an unmodified opinion. The Prospectus contains APMs and explicitly states that these APMs are not audited. Therefore the Adjusted EBITDA values in the Annual Report are supported by audited IFRS statements reconciled in notes, while the Prospectus repeats APMs and reconciliation tables but states they are not audited.
- Differences in reported Adjusted EBITDA between Prospectus six-month (30 June 2020) figures and Annual Report full-year 2020: Prospectus six-month Adjusted EBITDA for 30 June 2020 = 182.6m (NOKm) while Annual Report reports full-year 2020 Adjusted EBITDA = 390.841m (NOKk). These align logically (six-month vs full year), but note Annual Report FY2020 adjusted EBITDA is materially larger due to full year and different measurement bases (full year includes second half acquisitions/changes and share-based comp additions). Segment totals in Annual Report show larger adjusted EBITDA (390.842 by segments) matching the APM reconciliation.
- Adjustments composition: Both documents clearly list adjustments that define Adjusted EBITDA: M&A costs (consultancy/legal fees), restructuring costs (efficiency projects, start-ups, branding, severance/re-hiring extracted from payroll), and share-based compensation. Annual Report also includes share-based compensation as a material add-back in 2020 (34,711k). Prospectus shows share option program cost often zero in historical years but mentioned as adjustment. Both documents treat acquisition-related estimated contributions as management estimates (not audited), and include purchase price adjustments/earn-outs treated in finance lines.
- Pro forma use: Prospectus uses LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies for covenant testing and indicates pro forma adjustments in Capitalisation & Indebtedness section; Annual Report includes pro forma guidance in Board section (pro forma revenue and pro forma adjusted EBITDA margin for 2024) and large purchase price adjustments in cash flows (e.g., FY2020 purchase price adjustment of -147,902k). This indicates the company uses pro forma EBITDA in covenant and planning contexts; the Prospectus also references pro forma 'including synergies' — but the exact pro forma adjustments and supporting schedules are not included in the provided excerpts.

D. Any restatements / auditor notes that modify historical figures
- From the provided excerpts, no restatements or auditor modifications to historical EBITDA or Adjusted EBITDA are present. The independent auditor's report is unmodified and key audit matters focus on impairment of goodwill. The Prospectus flags that APMs are not audited and acquisition estimates are unaudited. The Annual Report shows earn-out adjustments and purchase price adjustments but these are disclosed not as restatements, rather as part of acquisition accounting and cashflow reporting.

E. Extracted text snippets and exact locations (short selection of exact quotes with locations):
