- Prospectus Section 10.7.1 table (excerpt_2 / excerpt_1): shows Adjusted EBITDA 182.6 (30 Jun 2020), 134.2 (30 Jun 2019), 307.5 (YE2019) (Location: Section 10.7 Tabulation)
- Prospectus footnotes (excerpt_2 and excerpt_3): detailed (a) and (b) descriptions for M&A activities costs and restructuring cost and other including amounts pulled from payroll/severance. (Location: Section 10.7 footnotes)
- Prospectus Covenant (excerpt_11 / excerpt_10): "... consolidated total net debt was 7.03 times LTM consolidated proforma EBITDA including synergies ..." (Location: Covenants section)
- Annual Report APM note (excerpt_12 / excerpt_11): "Adjusted EBITDA means EBITDA adjusted by expenses related to significant one-time, non-recurring events such as acquisitions and restructuring activities, legal advisors, and share-based compensation." and reconciliation showing Adjusted EBITDA 390,841 (2020). (Location: Note 25 APMs)
- Annual Report reconciliation (excerpt_11): "Operating profit (loss) ('EBIT') 22,218 ... EBITDA 293,607 ... Restructuring costs 47,400 ... Share-based compensation 34,711 ... Expenses related to acquisitions 15,123 ... Adjusted EBITDA 390,841" (Location: APM reconciliation)
- Auditor report (excerpt_15/16): unmodified opinion; Key Audit Matter: Impairment of goodwill; no auditor qualification regarding Adjusted EBITDA or restatements. (Location: Independent Auditor’s Report)

### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
- Methodological caution: Adjusted EBITDA is an APM (non-IFRS) and both documents warn that APMs are not audited and may be calculated differently between companies. The Prospectus explicitly states APMs "are not audited" whereas the Annual Report provides audited IFRS financial statements and reconciliations in the notes. For rigorous analysis or covenant calculation, rely on audited financial statement line items and the reconciliations in the Annual Report notes; treat prospectus APMs as management-presented and possibly unaudited snapshots (particularly six-month figures and management estimates for acquired entities).
